 "submission": {
  "summary": "F-12's oil fall in 2011-2013 was water taking over the well, not a loss of reservoir pressure. Liquid rate stayed near 5,000 Sm3/d while the choke opened to 100% and water cut rose from 72% to 95%, and field injection kept pace with voidage. Its water-oil ratio trend leaves about 189,000 Sm3 of oil before a 95% water cut (central estimate), with the 80% and 90% reference points already passed.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "F-12's oil rate fell while liquid stayed full and the choke opened, showing water taking capacity rather than depletion.",
    "detail": "Waterflood by_year: liquid 4,970 Sm3/d in 2011, 5,260 in 2012, 5,096 in 2013; choke 77% in 2011 to 100% in 2012 and 100% in 2013; water cut 0.7586 in 2011 to 0.9044 in 2013. Field voidage replacement ratio 1.02 in 2011, 1.02 in 2012, 1.03 in 2013 (near 1 = injection kept pace). Gauge failure since 2010-10-12 is sensor dead, not pressure collapse: 1,106 zero-days with 966 flowing days and 826,952 Sm3 oil produced after.",
    "evidence_ids": [
     "E3",
     "E4"
    ],
    "confidence": "inference",
    "numbers": [
     {
      "text": "4,970",
      "value": 4970,
