      "evidence_id": "E4"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Water cut rose from about 72% to 95% and oil rate fell from 1,444 to 268 Sm3/d over 2011-2013 while the well stayed on.",
    "detail": "Production monthly: 2011-01 oil_rate_per_producing_day 1444, water_cut 0.7232; 2013-12 oil_rate 268.25, water_cut 0.9467. Waterflood monthly confirms WOR 2.61 in 2011-01 to 17.78 in 2013-12. Oil regime change around 2010-07-18 had already shifted mean from 4,050 to 919 Sm3/d (-77%) with choke unchanged (54% -> 51%), so 2011-2013 is the steady water-driven tail after breakthrough (water cut >0.5 on 2010-06-04, >0.8 on 2012-02-14).",
