   {
    "claim": "The exponential decline fitted to 2011-2013 oil rate gives a steady fall consistent with water encroachment, not a pressure collapse.",
    "detail": "Best model exponential on 2011-01-01 to 2013-12-31: qi 1534 Sm3/d per producing day, di 0.5041 per year, b 0.0, n_points 886, r2_log 0.882, rmse_log 0.1635, residual_trend -0.006993, uptime 0.8058, no warnings. Other models: hyperbolic b 0.001 aic -3202 r2 0.8819; harmonic b 1.0 aic -2788 r2 0.8112. Liquid held while choke opened to 100% in same window, so decline is water taking well capacity.",
